# Flutter / Dart build artifacts (dischargeiq_mobile/)
# pubspec.lock is TRACKED on purpose (Work Plan v2 task 3.6: locked dependency
# versions across backend and client - the Dart counterpart of
# requirements.lock.txt).
dischargeiq_mobile/build/
dischargeiq_mobile/.dart_tool/
dischargeiq_mobile/.flutter-plugins
dischargeiq_mobile/.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# Claude Flow tool artifacts
.claude-flow/

# Video and archive artifacts
*.mp4
*.zip

# Design mockup / prototype files (not tracked source)
design-canvas.jsx
ios-frame.jsx
mobile-screens.jsx

# Presentation exports
presentation.html
presentation.md
"DischargeIQ Mobile.html"
DischargeIQ\ Mobile.html

# Research and handoff documents
SHADOW_STUDY.md
THERACARE_HANDOFF.md
docs/DischargeIQ_WorkPlan_v2.pdf
.gstack/

# Local-only archive of design mockups, demo videos, and superseded docs
_archive/

# Node dependencies (reinstall with npm install; package-lock.json is tracked)
node_modules/
.env.bak*
.env.bak-jul10
# The de-identified test corpus and the agent prose derived from it are NOT
# tracked (decision reversed 16 Aug 2026 - they were briefly committed on
# 14 Aug). Rebuild the corpus with scripts/build_mtsamples_corpus.py and the
# outputs with scripts/run_corpus_for_review.py; neither is authored here, and
# keeping clinical evaluation material out of the tree makes the pending
# handover to an LOF-controlled repository a decision about code alone.
#
# NOTE: untracking is not deletion. Both directories remain in history from
# the 14-15 Aug commits, so a clone can still retrieve them. If this
# repository is ever made public, or transferred under data-governance
# conditions, history has to be purged as a separate deliberate step.
test-data/mtsamples/
evaluation/corpus_outputs/

# The three generated demo fixtures at the top of test-data/ stay tracked on
# purpose: the beta kit ships them, scripts/verify_live_service.py drives
# them, and dischargeiq/tests/test_ingest.py parses one. They are ours and
# contain no patient material.
!test-data/*.pdf

# Documents kept out of the repo.
#
# Work plan PDFs are LOF deliverables that travel by email, not by git; the
# markdown in docs/deliverables/ is the version-controlled record.
docs/DischargeIQ_WorkPlan*.pdf

# CS 595 course artifacts under the old MedSynapse name. Coursework for IIT,
# not LOF deliverables, and binaries that bloat the history. Still on disk.
docs/*MedSynapse*
docs/CS595_*

# Office/binary docs generally - keep the repo reviewable as text.
docs/*.docx
docs/*.pptx

# Generated decks - rebuild with scripts/build_frank_deck.py
docs/*.pptx

# App screenshots for the deck - recapture from the emulator when needed
docs/deck-assets/

# Generated field card - rebuild with scripts/build_clinician_field_card.py
docs/CLINICIAN_FIELD_CARD.pdf

# On-device backups pulled by scripts/deploy_ios.sh before every install.
# These contain real analysed discharge documents and PDFs - never commit them
# (LOF rules bar clinical data in the repo, and this repo may become public).
device-backups/

# Android signing material. The keystore itself lives OUTSIDE this repo
# (~/.dischargeiq/), and key.properties carries its passwords - committing
# either would hand anyone the ability to sign a build as this app.
**/android/key.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
